Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||03-02-2000||03:21 PM||||Yes I was wondering if anyone on this board has a northstar fiero?  I get kit car and am on the web alott but I have never seen anyone with a design 1 fiero fiero.  Do they have a bad reputation or something like that?  They are pretty close in okc and I go through there every now and then and thought I might drop in on them, but as for anyone ever talking about them, I have never heard anything so can anyone enlighten me?  well thanks in advance if you can!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||03-02-2000||04:59 PM||||Got there website from Cobra <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com/</A>  Maybe he can give you some insight?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||03-02-2000||05:09 PM||||I believe the reason you don’t see many (any) is because they cost $8,000- $10,000 to do.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jhogans||03-02-2000||05:17 PM||||They were featured in one of the Kit Car magazines.  I will find out which one.  They quoted be a $15000 price tag for a Turnkey Northstar installation.  They also have a twin turbo in the works for the Northstar.  You will need to add about $6000 more to the price tag.  They believe the twin turbo will up the 300HP to over 400HP.  GOT DAMN!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||03-02-2000||06:07 PM||||Why spend that much? All you need is a Civic, with a couple of 6" exhaust tips, some racing stripes.. bright colored paint.. huge wing.. cut springs.. big wheels.. might be able to hit 500hp. maybe 525hp with a K&N filter and some stickers.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>j/k.. heh.. the Design 1 setup sounds sweet.. too expensive for me, but very cool.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pherder||03-02-2000||06:43 PM||||I know the engineer that developed the kit that Designone sells.  His name is John Austin of Fort Worth, TX.  Before he put the N* in his 88 GT, he had a LT-1 in it.  <P>I have seen the prototype car (the 88 GT) with the N* in it and it looks like the factory put it there!  The car is super fast even with the N* stock!.  The engine/transaxle assembly is from a Cadillac (of course) and is mounted EXACTLY the same as if in the Cadillac.  ALL rubber mounted (unlike most kits that mount the assembly solid) using the stock Cadillac mounts.<P>Kevin Leslie (Designone) is the one behind the Turbo kits for the 2.8 V6 and has the knowledge to redesign the PROM to work in the Fiero (with or without the turbos) and to build the wiring harness.  Together with John, they have an impressive install.<P>Paul||||reg||14
Z||000007||mrfiero||03-02-2000||09:56 PM||||I know someone getting a N* in their Fiero right now.  Design One is doing the job and as Paul said, they do excellent work and it looks like it was a factory install.<P>I'm sure a lot of people get sticker shocked when they hear how much they charge, but it is well worth it (if you're in the market for a N*) as it is a very professional job.....not a hack job.  <P>Evidently the folks at Design One (maybe it's Kevin?) have a basically stock '85 GT with a N* that they "prowl" the streets in looking for prey.  My friend said they embarassed a Porsche 911 on a test drive.  I can't imagine what it would be like with the turbo set-up.<P>The good news for me is I get to drive his car when it's finished!  It'll be worth the drive to OKC from Denver.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000008||jhogans||03-02-2000||11:40 PM||||When I hit the lottery, I will definetly do  the NorthStar install with the Twin Turbo.<P>BTW, what do you mean when you say, "The engine/transaxle assembly"?  I have a 5spd transmission.  Does that mean it will get replaced with an automatic transmission.||||reg||1
Z||000009||pherder||03-03-2000||07:28 PM||||With Designone's kit, they only use the Cadillac auto transaxle.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>The prototype 88 GT was a 5 speed and he converted it over to an auto.<P>Paul||||reg||9
